{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BlochFiveTerm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BlochFiveTerm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Bloch.three_smul_wedge_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Bloch.three_smul_wedge_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BlochFiveTerm.lean#L130-L142","doc":"**A multiplicative dependence `2·u = 3·v` forces `w u v` to be 3-torsion.**\n\nApplied with `u = (y)`, `v = (1−y)` in `F^×` (additively), this says the\n`d`-image of a 5₂ saddle root is 3-torsion in `Λ²(F^×)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Bloch.wedge_five_term_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Bloch.wedge_five_term_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BlochFiveTerm.lean#L89-L110","doc":"**`Σᵢ (zᵢ) ∧ (1−zᵢ) = 0` for the five-term relation.**\n\n`w` is any biadditive alternating pairing; `aᵢ` are the (additively written)\narguments, and the hypothesis `w x (y + z) = w x y + w x z` together with\n`w x y + w y x = 0` is exactly what `Λ²` supplies. The five `y`-arguments are\nthe sums `aᵢ₋₁ + aᵢ₊₁`, the additive form of `1 − zᵢ = zᵢ₋₁·zᵢ₊₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Bloch.lyness_period_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Bloch.lyness_period_five","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BlochFiveTerm.lean#L63-L71","doc":"**The cyclic five-term relation has period 5**: `z₆ = z₁`.\n\nThe survey states this as \"implies by a short calculation that they have\nperiod 5\" (`library/arxiv-2304.12545v1/2304.12545v1.pdf` §3). This is that calculation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Bloch.lyness_z5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Bloch.lyness_z5","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BlochFiveTerm.lean#L55-L61","doc":"`z₅ = (1 − a)/b` in the cyclic five-term recurrence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Bloch.lyness_z4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Bloch.lyness_z4","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BlochFiveTerm.lean#L49-L53","doc":"`z₄ = (a + b − 1)/(ab)` in the cyclic five-term recurrence. ","signatureChunk":0}]}